# Goal Synchronization Analysis: Universal Skeleton vs. OrchLayer

This analysis details how the implemented "Universal Skeleton" aligns with and supports the core goals of the "OrchLayer" project.

## Core Goal Alignment

| OrchLayer Principle | Implementation in Universal Skeleton |
|---------------------|---------------------------------------|
| **Project-First Continuity** | Use of [AGENTS.md](file:///c:/dev/git-src/OrchLayerAI/AGENTS.md) and `docs/` files ensures that any agent (past, present, or future) starts with the same project context. |
| **Stateless Honesty** | [AGENTS.md](file:///c:/dev/git-src/OrchLayerAI/AGENTS.md) explicitly forbids "fake completion" and "pretending hidden memory exists," forcing agents to verify repo state. |
| **Knowledge Minimalism** | The structure separates core schemas (`00_Project-Core`) from platform-specific implementation (`10`, `20`, `30` folders). |
| **Explicit Handoffs** | The [docs/WORKFLOW.md](file:///c:/dev/git-src/OrchLayerAI/docs/WORKFLOW.md) and [docs/CHANGELOG-TRACKER.md](file:///c:/dev/git-src/OrchLayerAI/docs/CHANGELOG-TRACKER.md) provide a human-readable trace of handoffs and changes. |
| **Tool Realism** | The [REPO-MAP.md](file:///c:/dev/git-src/OrchLayerAI/docs/REPO-MAP.md) and `decisions-log.md` document actual tool constraints and choices made during execution. |

## Component Interaction Map

```mermaid
graph TD
    User((User)) -- Decision/Priority --> Orchestrator[In-app Orchestrator]
    Orchestrator -- Task Brief --> FieldAI[Field AI Environment]
    FieldAI -- Return Packet --> Orchestrator
    
    subgraph Repo Structure
        Core[00_Project-Core: Schemas/Rules]
        Adapters[10/20/30_Adapters: Tool Configs]
        Docs[docs/: State/Workflow]
        Agents[AGENTS.md: Root Policy]
    end
    
    FieldAI -- Reads --> Core
    FieldAI -- Reads --> Agents
    FieldAI -- Updates --> Docs
    FieldAI -- Uses --> Adapters
```

## Synergy Findings

The Universal Skeleton acts as the "Observer/Actor" layer for OrchLayer. By providing a fixed documentation and policy structure ([AGENTS.md](file:///c:/dev/git-src/OrchLayerAI/AGENTS.md), `docs/`), it ensures that the Field AI environment (e.g., this agent) adheres to the L1 orchestration patterns without requiring the Orchestrator to repeat rules in every prompt.

